name:
  type: string
  unique: true
  id: true

uri:
  type: uri
  arity: 0..1
  description: |
    Path to an external feature definition file (relative to the cluster
    YAML or absolute).  When supplied the file is loaded and merged with
    any inline fields — inline values take precedence over the file.

    Using `uri` makes the `name` and `labels` fields optional: they can be
    omitted and will be taken from the referenced file instead.

    This is the primary mechanism for sharing and reusing feature
    definitions across multiple clusters.

    Example (URI only — name and labels come from the file):
      - uri: ./features/prometheus.yaml

    Example (URI with name override):
      - name: my-prometheus
        uri: ./features/prometheus.yaml

labels:
  type: string
  arity: 1..*
  description: |
    Label(s) used to select the host(s) onto which to install this feature.

    A host is targeted when it carries at least one of these labels.

    **Label absorption**: when none of the cluster's hosts carry a matching
    label, the feature is instead deployed to every sole node (controllers
    running in --single mode).  This lets sole nodes act as a catch-all for
    features that haven't been explicitly routed yet.  Once a dedicated
    non-controller host with a matching label is added to the cluster, the
    explicit match takes precedence and the sole node no longer receives
    the feature.

    Required for inline feature definitions.  May be omitted when `uri` is
    provided and the referenced file contains the labels.

singleton:
  type: boolean
  arity: 0..1
  description: |
    When true, the feature is deployed to exactly one matching node
    (the first in cluster-definition order) instead of every node that
    carries a matching label.

    Use this for features that must run as a single instance across the
    cluster — for example a shared database, a unique message broker, or
    any workload where running on multiple nodes simultaneously would
    cause conflicts or data duplication.

    Defaults to false (feature is deployed to all matching nodes).

locations:
  type: uri
  arity: 0..*
  description: |
    Filepaths containing necessary installation
    scripts and configurations for deployment

install-cmds:
  type: bash
  arity: 0..*
  description: |
    List of installation commands. Runs
    sequentially. All filepaths defined under
    `locations` are mounted in the execution
    directory throughout deployment only

init-cmds:
  type: bash
  arity: 0..*
  description: |
    List of initialization commands, executed
    once, needed to execute the feature at
    runtime


  